before we go we want to take a moment to  honor someone who was an instrumental  part of our cbs news family longtime  photojournalist george christian died  over the weekend  throughout his more than 40-year career  he helped us document iconic moments all  over the world from the fall of the  berlin wall to nelson mandela's release  from prison  and his election as south africa's  president  christian was on air force one with  president bush on 9 11 covered  presidents clinton clinton's time in  office and witnessed president nixon's  resignation he talked about that in an  interview with chip reid back in 2014.  i've been fortunate enough to be in  places where i would have paid cbs to be  there  this was one of them and i would have  paid a lot and i think a lot of people  would you had a front row seat on  history i had a front row seat i wasn't  sitting there  i was standing hiding behind the  camera george christian earned an emmy  award and a special lifetime achievement  award from the radio and television  correspondents association for all of  his  incredible work our hearts go out to his  family george shot the first piece i  ever did for cbs news and he was on the  head on camera for face the nation he  was a good he was a man he was a kind  and talented guy part of the fun of  going to the washington bureau is you  get to see him his smiling face and he  was always so welcoming and whenever you  see  somebody like that and you hear their  voice it just sort of brings you back  and he's like so you know so many we  work with who  those of you out there don't see yeah  but they make us who we are and what we  are not just on tv but he george  christian was a good man who made you  better even when you weren't on tv what  a wonderful career and what a great  advertisement for the profession you  know berlin wall south africa multiple  presidents dixon resignation this  incredible life  and to see him in his suit and tie  standing behind the camera  i always say i always think that's nice  george you will be missed our  condolences again to your family
 

